\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Scalar sign links preserve the geometric right action}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{Change the coefficient fiber in the
[geometric right action](fdip-00VK) to #{k} with the sign
representation of #{C_2}, and take #{N=1}. Every represented
link #{u_i} satisfies #{u_i^{-1}=u_i}. The pullback and its
inverse are both multiplication by #{u_i}, so
##{\extD_U=\sum_i(u_i-1)(e_i\wedge+e_i\cdot).}
Each exterior operator in this sum is left Clifford
multiplication. Hence it commutes with every geometric
right multiplication. Scalar gauges commute as well.
At trivial links the displayed operator is zero. Thus the
surviving right actions depend on the coefficient
representation, even on one site.}
